WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.179
Every town has its urban legends.

00:00:03.179 --> 00:00:09.190
An unnatural abomination with the body of
an animal and the head of a human lurking

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:10.190
the forests.

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:12.900
A bridge said to curse any who stand under
it in the dead of night.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:18.039
A lurking serial killer continuing his crimes
from beyond the grave.

00:00:18.039 --> 00:00:22.210
You might be familiar with the hook-man, a
chilling tale about a young couple finding

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.960
a man’s hooked-hand hanging on the back
of their car.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:31.800
Or tales about mysterious clowns being sighted
in the woods outside of suburban areas.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:36.190
Over time, the truth behind an urban legend
will become muddled, and the original story

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:40.250
might change countless times before emerging
in its present form.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:46.210
They might entertain us, they sometimes might
even scare us, but all urban legends feed

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.949
on the tiny sliver that they might be true.

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:55.149
That voice inside your head telling you that
it might not be just a story designed to scare

00:00:55.149 --> 00:01:00.629
you, and that there are some aspects of the
world that are truly unknown.

00:01:00.629 --> 00:01:06.220
And most of all, you, the average person,
can get caught up in this world, forced into

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:08.640
it against your will by pure chance.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:15.080
A deranged killer, an unknown sea creature
lurking in a lake, a curse, a poorly understood

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.970
creature never before seen by science.

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:22.970
All of these images conjure up fear, but when
combined with the personalized nature of an

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:28.921
urban legend, which adds familiar places,
names, and situations to the mix, it’s no

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:31.610
wonder why these stories take off.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:35.840
Rodney Hallow’s town, the name of which
has been scrubbed from all documentation by

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:40.930
the Foundation, was no different in that it
had its own share of urban legends.

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:45.159
Even though the town’s name is lost due
to the SCP Foundation wiping its name from

00:01:45.159 --> 00:01:51.430
official documentation, know that Rodney was
an average teenager, living an average life,

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:54.320
and doing average things a person his age
might do.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:59.479
And that included taking his friends up on
dares that he might regret later, dares pertaining

00:01:59.479 --> 00:02:01.930
to those urban legends.

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:05.700
Kids daring one another to do something like
this is nothing new.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:09.350
Whether it’s saying ‘bloody mary’ 3
times in a row before a bathroom mirror in

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:13.810
the dark, or taking a trip to an abandoned
building and staying the night there, you

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:18.980
should be undoubtedly familiar with how these
things work, and how easy it is to get a susceptible

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:20.940
young mind to do them.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.350
Who wants to risk an encounter with the supernatural?

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:29.970
Well, people who don’t want to chicken out
in front of their friends, of course!

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:34.840
Getting cursed by a ghost or the more realistic
possibility of accidentally injuring yourself

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:39.720
while exploring an abandoned area is nothing
compared to the feeling of satisfaction that

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:45.900
comes from looking cool in front of your friends,
at least, that rings true when you’re 14

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:46.900
years old.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:49.480
But Rodney Hallow was above that.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:53.680
He was, more than anything else, a scaredy
cat to his core.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:58.350
No amount of peer pressure could make him
fold, because his fears outweighed his social

00:02:58.350 --> 00:02:59.350
capital.

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:04.340
If Rodney was afraid of it, his friends knew
there was no chance of getting him near it.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.680
In a way, it was admirable.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:11.290
He could be offered money, food, literally
anything he wanted, and if Rodney didn’t

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.370
want to do it, he wouldn’t.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:16.780
Not just that, but he felt like he physically
couldn’t.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:20.841
It was like every bone in his body would freeze
up, his heart would start beating intensely,

00:03:20.841 --> 00:03:24.170
and he would internally panic.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:28.560
It was a regular feeling of fear, sure, but
Rodney felt it often.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:34.370
A fear of exams, a fear of the future, snakes,
spiders, open windows at night.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:38.840
Rodney was always overthinking things, and
his fears were well known among the small

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:41.330
circle he associated himself with.

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:45.220
Naturally, Rodney’s friends acted their
age, and spent a lot of time trying to come

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:49.340
up with new and exciting ways to scare the
daylights out of the poor kid.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:53.700
This could be playing pranks on him, giving
Rodney phone calls from hidden numbers, or

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.920
trying to get him to watch horror movies.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.840
It was getting to the point where Rodney was
more annoyed than anything else, and he was

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:03.260
beginning to heavily reconsider who he hung
out with.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:08.420
But if there was one person who could convince
Rodney to do something, it was Clair, a girl

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:11.340
in his class he had a tiny bit of a crush
on.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:15.870
And by a tiny bit, we mean that Rodney was
so willing to make himself look good in front

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:21.570
of Clair that he willingly accompanied his
friends to a supposedly haunted house located

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:24.780
in a rural area just outside of town.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:29.880
This was Rodney’s town’s urban legend,
and while it wasn’t well-known, this broken-down

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:34.440
house was slowly gaining a reputation among
the town’s youth as a gateway between the

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.940
realm of the living and the dead.

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:41.190
The lore varied depending on who you asked,
but it was said to be haunted by the spirit

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:46.250
of a puppet-maker, who was experimenting with
making puppets out of human bodies.

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:50.530
His reclusive nature and isolated lifestyle
meant that his crimes and experiments went

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:55.710
unnoticed until his death, when law enforcement
seized the house and cleared out hundreds

00:04:55.710 --> 00:05:00.160
of mutilated, half-human, half-wooden puppet
creations.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:04.160
Of course, this was all just hearsay, and
there was no actual proof beyond what was

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.470
said at Rodney’s lunchtable.

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:11.100
But as seasoned viewers of this channel know,
in the world of the SCP Foundation, there

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:15.730
is always a kernel of truth in even the slightest
story of the unknown.

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:17.980
The outline of Rodney’s dare was simple.

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:22.910
He and Clair would have to spend an hour inside
the house alone, while his friends waited

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:24.650
for him outside of it.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:26.170
Pretty great friends, huh?

00:05:26.170 --> 00:05:30.360
Under any other circumstances, Rodney would
have refused to even leave his house that

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:34.740
night, but the prospects of looking good in
front of Clair were too tempting for even

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:37.350
the scardiest of scaredy-cats to pass up.

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:42.270
Besides, if he played it cool, he could use
this as a way to talk to Clair and actually

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:43.770
get to know her a bit better.

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:45.840
They’d have a whole hour together!

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:51.960
Just… an hour inside a dark, dilapidated
house occupied by a puppet-maker serial killer’s

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:52.960
ghost.

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:58.190
Still, Rodney clenched his fist and grit his
teeth, determined to shake off his reputation

00:05:58.190 --> 00:05:59.190
as a wimp.

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:03.110
The house stood before him, and Clair stood
beside him.

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:08.280
They moved forward together, much to the chuckling
and stifled laughter of the kids behind them,

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:12.590
and with a forceful jiggling of the locked
doorknob using a makeshift lockpick made of

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:16.800
a paperclip and a piece of metal, they entered
the house.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:20.320
The inside was dark, but that much was to
be expected.

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:25.350
As soon as the two entered, the door slammed
itself shut, and a clicking sound was heard,

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:27.260
indicating that it was now locked.

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:29.410
Immediately, Rodney knew something was wrong.

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:34.550
He had a feeling he would see some unexplainable
things, but he didn’t expect one to occur

00:06:34.550 --> 00:06:36.630
immediately after he entered.

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:39.080
The door just slammed itself shut.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:43.000
Clair turned back and attempted to open it,
but she had no luck.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:47.770
Rodney, in what he felt was a smooth move,
told her to calm down, and that when their

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:51.660
hour was eventually up, they could just break
through a window to get out.

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:55.560
This seemed to work, and Clair hesitantly
calmed herself.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:07:00.700
The interior of the house was old, done in
a baroque style unfitting of the unimpressive

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:01.700
exterior.

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:06.330
A spiraling staircase, a few paintings, armchairs
in front of a fireplace.

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:10.810
It was clear that whoever lived here, if they
didn’t have money, they certainly had access

00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:12.840
to skilled craftsmanship.

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:17.090
There were faint pockets of light in the distance,
coming from candles positioned sparsely throughout

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:18.090
the home.

00:07:18.090 --> 00:07:22.820
The two began to explore, not content to stay
in any one place for too long.

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:26.680
The frightened duo came to an ornate, yet
run-down kitchen.

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:31.110
Their footsteps creaked with every movement,
but when they stopped, they noticed that the

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:33.040
stepping sounds didn’t.

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:35.600
Rodney began to panic, as he was used to.

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:39.470
Keeping a cool head in this situation was
next to impossible.

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:43.140
Slow stepping sounds, coming from various
parts of the house.

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:46.530
They moved closer, practically clinging to
each other.

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:51.420
If Rodney wasn’t so scared, this would have
been an ideal situation, but he couldn’t

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:52.560
even appreciate it.

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:56.510
The footsteps didn’t grow louder, they just
increased in number.

00:07:56.510 --> 00:08:01.460
Slow, moving steps coming from above, below,
and beside them.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:07.050
And then, in the distance, from the poorly-lit
hallway in front of them, Rodney saw a shape.

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:12.060
A jerkily-moving, barely-visible shape, but
it was approaching them.

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:16.490
Clair saw it too, and the two ran out of the
kitchen and back to the front of the house.

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:20.380
They banged on the door, begging and screaming
for their friends to let them back out, but

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:22.140
there was no response.

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:26.400
They tried to break open a window, but they
physically found themselves unable to damage

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:27.400
the house.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:32.410
It was as if they wanted to protect it instead
of damage it, even though both of them knew

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:37.560
they absolutely wanted to break a window and
run out of the house as fast as possible.

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:42.260
The figure was approaching, and the footsteps
didn’t stop either.

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:46.260
It was then that Rodney caught a glimpse of
the figure that was trailing them, a picture

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:49.089
only visible due to the brief flash of candle-light.

00:08:49.089 --> 00:08:55.589
It was a sunken, hollowed out corpse, with
button-eyes and rust-brown skin.

00:08:55.589 --> 00:09:00.150
As soon as it moved beyond the candle, the
entity was difficult to see again, but Rodney

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:03.770
was unable to scrub that brief image from
his mind.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:08.080
It jerked towards them, slow step by slow
step.

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:12.330
And then, it lunged forward at a frighteningly
fast, unnatural speed.

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:13.340
The two screamed.

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:16.410
Rodney fell to the floor, passed out in fear.

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:19.120
And then everything went quiet.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:23.660
Rodney and Clair were just another disappearance
that had a connection to that abandoned house,

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:28.330
and when the local police force launched an
investigation, they compiled over 20 cases

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:33.370
of teenagers from ages 12 to 17 that went
missing as a result of visiting the abandoned

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:35.300
home over the past decade.

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:40.230
A small team of law enforcement was dispatched
to inspect and investigate the home in-person,

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:42.010
but they did not return.

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:46.450
It was at this point when the incident caught
the attention of the SCP Foundation, who overtook

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:51.520
the investigation and launched a massive cover
story that involved a mass amnesticization

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:56.200
of law enforcement officers and relatives
of the missing persons, as well as a planting

00:09:56.200 --> 00:10:00.760
of a memetic agent in the area that induced
brain patterns that would discourage the town’s

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:05.010
residents from talking about or spreading
the urban legend of the house.

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:09.630
The Foundation quickly established containment
procedures and a security perimeter was set

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:11.360
up around the house.

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:16.870
After a cursory, preliminary batch of research
and testing, the house was decidedly anomalous,

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:23.320
and was given the designation of SCP-1098-RU,
labeled as such due to the investigation taking

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:29.460
place in Russia and being handled by the Russian
branch of the SCP Foundation.

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:34.060
SCP-1098-RU’s containment procedures, on
top of the cover story that was put into place

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:39.020
to discourage and suppress the spread of the
urban legend, were effective in deterring

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:41.300
civilians from entering the area.

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:46.560
Originally, the city administration had proposed
to destroy and dismantle the house years ago,

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:51.180
but the building’s demolition was constantly
postponed by bureaucratic red tape.

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:56.420
The entirety of the area was fenced in, and
patrolled by an armed security detail at all

00:10:56.420 --> 00:11:00.410
hours, with the guards shifting positions
every six hours.

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:05.030
If any civilians attempted to enter, they
would be arrested and interrogated, with the

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:07.040
use of amnestics permitted.

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:12.279
If anything regarding SCP-1098-RU were to
change, the guards would have to report it

00:11:12.279 --> 00:11:15.620
to Site-7 and wait for further instruction.

00:11:15.620 --> 00:11:21.310
From the Foundation’s research, it was determined
that SCP-1098-RU was a difficult anomaly to

00:11:21.310 --> 00:11:22.310
analyze.

00:11:22.310 --> 00:11:25.590
The house’s primary anomalous effect was
a protective one.

00:11:25.590 --> 00:11:31.490
All of the windows and the front door of SCP-1098-RU
were automatically locked, and if someone

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:36.490
attempted to enter the house via physically
damaging one of these spots, or anywhere else

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:40.160
on the house, they would find themselves unable
to do so.

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:47.040
Instead, they would feel motivated to protect
SCP-1098-RU, and prevent any damage to it.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:51.590
This, of course, wouldn’t override any other
preexisting feelings toward the house, so

00:11:51.590 --> 00:11:56.680
as we saw in Rodney’s case, this can result
in a conflict of interest where a victim wanted

00:11:56.680 --> 00:12:01.060
to escape, but was unable to due to the house’s
protective trap.

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:07.000
This effect is only active when a person is
within at least 50 meters of SCP-1098-RU,

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:11.540
which explains why the plans for the house’s
demolition were plotted, but actually unable

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:12.950
to be carried out.

00:12:12.950 --> 00:12:19.050
The only way to enter SCP-1098 is the house’s
front door, through use of a lockpicking device

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:21.490
or another way to break the door’s lock.

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:26.589
Upon entry, the door will close automatically,
lock itself from the outside, and is unable

00:12:26.589 --> 00:12:28.880
to be opened for the next hour.

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:33.550
Attempts to break into the house before this
hour is through are futile, as the anomaly’s

00:12:33.550 --> 00:12:37.750
protective measures will trigger in order
to prevent damage coming from the house.

00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:43.520
The home’s origins are presently unknown,
as the Foundation is still investigating them,

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:48.280
but the urban legend of the puppet-maker who
turned his victims into puppets may hold some

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:49.550
credence.

00:12:49.550 --> 00:12:55.110
SCP-1098-1 is an entity that has been nicknamed
the Master of Puppets, and you’re about

00:12:55.110 --> 00:12:56.420
to see why.

00:12:56.420 --> 00:13:00.930
But the entity is a self-containing spirit,
believed to be the cause of most of the anomalous

00:13:00.930 --> 00:13:02.800
phenomena within the house.

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:07.930
The Foundation hasn’t found a way to contact
or research the -1 entity beyond observing

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:13.040
the brief appearances of it during testing,
so information on the anomaly is limited to

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:14.310
what’s been observed.

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:18.960
And that would be candles that are unable
to be extinguished or replaced, strange glows

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:23.600
of light emerging from the cracks in sealed
windows and walls, hallucinations based on

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:28.250
the fears of the victims trapped inside, and
the sound of slow, approaching steps from

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:29.820
throughout the house.

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:34.130
These steps are unable to be recorded using
audio devices, but the Foundation has reason

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:36.590
to believe they’re produced by the entity
itself.

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:40.370
Still, there’s a lot of mystery surrounding
SCP-1098.

00:13:40.370 --> 00:13:41.880
Where did it come from?

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:44.900
What is the SCP-1098-1 entity?

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:49.210
And most importantly, where do the corpses
of its victims go?

00:13:49.210 --> 00:13:51.290
That one is easy to answer.

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:56.690
The bodies of those who die inside SCP-1098
will be preserved by the entity, and altered

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:59.450
to take on the appearance of puppets.

00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:04.890
Their eyes will be removed and long, thick
threads will be sewn into their extremities.

00:14:04.890 --> 00:14:09.149
But what does SCP-1098-RU need these puppets
for?

00:14:09.149 --> 00:14:13.500
A look into the Foundation’s initial research
documents regarding the house may provide

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:14.560
the answer.

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:20.089
The Foundation’s exploration of SCP-1098-RU
occurred shortly after the object was put

00:14:20.089 --> 00:14:25.720
into containment, and remains the primary
source of information on how the anomaly functions

00:14:25.720 --> 00:14:27.980
and how its intricacies work.

00:14:27.980 --> 00:14:32.130
The first test involved a remote controlled
drone equipped with recording equipment, the

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:37.440
Foundation’s safest way to observe hostile,
unknown anomalous territory from a distance.

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:40.830
The drone entered, and was quickly locked
inside the house.

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:45.630
As it proceeded, it found several damaged,
altered corpses of missing persons in various

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:47.200
rooms of the house.

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:52.520
The bodies were missing their eyes, and all
had thick strings sewn onto them, with stitch

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:55.110
marks on the chest and face areas.

00:14:55.110 --> 00:14:58.940
Strangely, the bodies weren’t decomposed
at all, despite some of the corpses being

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:01.740
identified as being people who disappeared
months ago.

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:04.670
The drone’s survey also found several objects
of interest.

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:10.209
A set of surgical knives, threads, needles,
and a prosthetic, artificial eye.

00:15:10.209 --> 00:15:15.100
While the drone didn’t detect the -1 entity,
Foundation researchers could only speculate

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:19.640
as to where and what these objects were used
for, and by who.

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:23.290
The second test involved sending a D-Class
personnel into the building.

00:15:23.290 --> 00:15:27.530
He was supplied with a flashlight and recording
equipment, and was tasked with reexamining

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:29.339
the first floor of the house.

00:15:29.339 --> 00:15:33.330
The only difference the D-Class observed from
the drone exploration was that the candles

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:38.690
were clearly replaced by newer ones, indicating
that someone had changed them.

00:15:38.690 --> 00:15:42.640
Footsteps were heard throughout the home,
sometimes in areas that the D-Class had just

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:44.050
emerged from.

00:15:44.050 --> 00:15:48.290
Upon re-entering one room to investigate,
the D-Class was ordered to take a surgical

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:50.790
knife back to command for further study.

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:56.010
However, as soon as he lifted the knife, communication
immediately cut off, and the Foundation was

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:57.990
unable to re-establish contact.

00:15:57.990 --> 00:16:03.000
A third test was held shortly after to determine
what happened to the D-Class, as well as explore

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:08.190
the second floor of SCP-1098, this time using
another remote controlled drone.

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:12.950
The drone found that the house, on its second
floor, had a sewing workshop, filled with

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:18.329
all of the materials you would expect to find
in such, including threads, machinery, and

00:16:18.329 --> 00:16:19.329
tools.

00:16:19.329 --> 00:16:24.209
Multiple corpses were found, all dressed in
18th century clothes, their eyes replaced

00:16:24.209 --> 00:16:28.649
with artificial ones, and with strings sewn
into their bodies.

00:16:28.649 --> 00:16:33.269
Upon the drone’s return, communication was
cut off yet again, and when the hour period

00:16:33.269 --> 00:16:36.620
was up and the house’s door opened, there
was no sign of it anywhere.

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:43.000
The fourth test into SCP-1098 involved another
D-Class personnel, who was instructed to attempt

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:46.149
to leave the building before an hour passed.

00:16:46.149 --> 00:16:51.070
After entering, the D-Class reported a throbbing
headache and immediate pressure in his ears.

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:55.529
He reported that someone was crying in the
farthest room on the first floor, but the

00:16:55.529 --> 00:16:57.950
equipment couldn’t pick anything up.

00:16:57.950 --> 00:17:03.070
After entering, he reported that he saw a
little girl, wearing an old-fashioned dress,

00:17:03.070 --> 00:17:08.160
and she was dancing and crying, being pulled
upward into motion by the strings that were

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:09.909
sewn onto her back.

00:17:09.909 --> 00:17:14.970
These strings, on camera, were completely
invisible to the Foundation, leading the command

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:18.389
to believe that the D-Class was experiencing
hallucinations.

00:17:18.389 --> 00:17:22.610
The D-Class simply stood and observed, almost
transfixed by the girl.

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:27.059
He remarked that it seemed like the strings
stretched on forever, and that there was no

00:17:27.059 --> 00:17:31.019
ceiling, even though the Foundation could
clearly see the ceiling of the room on the

00:17:31.019 --> 00:17:32.019
camera.

00:17:32.019 --> 00:17:36.600
After 5 minutes of silence and observation,
a startling clap was heard as the camera’s

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:37.879
visuals cut out.

00:17:37.879 --> 00:17:41.489
And then, a male voice, but not that of the
D-Class, spoke:

00:17:41.489 --> 00:17:45.889
“In perficientur est pretium.”

00:17:45.889 --> 00:17:52.529
When translated from latin to english, it
read: “The performance must be paid for”.

00:17:52.529 --> 00:17:58.360
After this, the Foundation put a stop to all
further experimentation with SCP-1098-RU,

00:17:58.360 --> 00:18:00.720
content with the data they had gained.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:06.559
Until the Foundation gains more information
about SCP-1098 and the mysterious entity inside,

00:18:06.559 --> 00:18:11.769
sending more resources in will only result
in them meeting a gruesome demise.

00:18:11.769 --> 00:18:16.650
Until then, they can only speculate about
the true nature of the entity known as the

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:18.869
Master of Puppets.

00:18:18.869 --> 00:18:25.649
Now go check out “SCP-2696 Haunted Victorian
Mansion” and “SCP-4153 - Haunted House

00:18:25.649 --> 00:18:31.850
Horror - It Came from Site-9!” for more
anomalous haunted houses from SCP Explained!

